# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Critical concepts {#critical-concepts}"
msgstr "Konsep kritis {#critical-concepts}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum information cannot be copied or \"cloned\".\n"
msgstr "Informasi kuantum tidak dapat disalin atau \"dikloning\".\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You *can* repeat the same preparation process to make an ensemble of quantum"
" states which are all the same, or nearly the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu *bisa* mengulangi proses persiapan yang sama untuk membuat ensembel "
"keadaan kuantum yang semuanya sama, atau hampir sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An encryption/decryption key (a one-time pad) can be shared between two "
"friends using quantum states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kunci enkripsi/dekripsi (one-time pad) bisa dibagikan antara dua teman "
"menggunakan keadaan kuantum.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two friends randomly choosing a measurement basis means that half the time "
"they will choose differently, and will have to toss out the information on "
"those qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua teman yang memilih basis pengukuran secara acak berarti setengah dari "
"waktu mereka akan memilih berbeda, dan harus membuang informasi pada qubit-"
"qubit tersebut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The random choice of measurement basis also ensures that an eavesdropper "
"cannot know the initial state prepared, and thus cannot recreate the sent "
"state. This ensures that the eavesdropping will be detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilihan basis pengukuran yang acak juga memastikan bahwa penyadap tidak "
"dapat mengetahui keadaan awal yang disiapkan, dan dengan demikian tidak "
"dapat merekonstruksi keadaan yang dikirim. Ini memastikan penyadapan akan "
"terdeteksi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "T/F questions {#tf-questions}"
msgstr "Pertanyaan B/S {#tf-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F In quantum key distribution, the two communicating partners measure each"
" qubit in the same basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"B/S Dalam distribusi kunci kuantum, dua mitra yang berkomunikasi mengukur "
"setiap qubit dalam basis yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F An eavesdropper intercepting quantum information in QKD is prevented by "
"the laws of nature from copying the quantum state they intercept.\n"
msgstr ""
"B/S Seorang penyadap yang mencegat informasi kuantum dalam QKD dicegah oleh "
"hukum alam untuk menyalin keadaan kuantum yang mereka cegat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"T/F A one-time pad is a key for encrypting/decrypting secure messages in "
"which a particular encoding scheme is used only once, for a single piece of "
"information (like one letter of the alphabet).\n"
msgstr ""
"B/S One-time pad adalah kunci untuk mengenkripsi/mendekripsi pesan aman di "
"mana skema pengkodean tertentu hanya digunakan sekali, untuk satu bagian "
"informasi (seperti satu huruf alfabet).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "MC questions {#mc-questions}"
msgstr "Pertanyaan PG {#mc-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Select the option that best completes the statement. As described in this "
"module, a one-time pad is a set of encryption/decryption keys that is "
"used...\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilih opsi yang paling tepat melengkapi pernyataan berikut. Seperti yang "
"dijelaskan dalam modul ini, one-time pad adalah sekumpulan kunci "
"enkripsi/dekripsi yang digunakan...\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "a. Only once for a single piece of information, like a single letter.\n"
msgstr "a. Hanya sekali untuk satu bagian informasi, seperti satu huruf.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "b. Only once for a single message.\n"
msgstr "b. Hanya sekali untuk satu pesan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "c. Only once for a set period of time, like a day.\n"
msgstr "c. Hanya sekali untuk periode waktu tertentu, seperti satu hari.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "d. Until there is evidence of eavesdropping.\n"
msgstr "d. Sampai ada bukti penyadapan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume Alice and Bob choose their measurement bases randomly. They measure. "
"Then they share their measurement bases, and keep only the bits of "
"information from cases where they used the same basis. Up to some random "
"fluctuation, approximately what percentage of their qubits should yield "
"usable bits of information?\n"
msgstr ""
"Asumsikan Alice dan Bob memilih basis pengukuran mereka secara acak. Mereka "
"melakukan pengukuran. Kemudian mereka berbagi basis pengukuran, dan hanya "
"menyimpan bit informasi dari kasus-kasus di mana mereka menggunakan basis "
"yang sama. Dengan mempertimbangkan fluktuasi acak, kira-kira berapa persen "
"qubit mereka yang menghasilkan bit informasi yang dapat digunakan?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "a. 100%\n"
msgstr "a. 100%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "b. 50%\n"
msgstr "b. 50%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "c. 25%\n"
msgstr "c. 25%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "d. 12.5%\n"
msgstr "d. 12,5%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "e. 0%\n"
msgstr "e. 0%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob select cases in which they used the same measurement "
"bases, what percentage of those bits of information should match, if quantum"
" noise and errors were negligible?\n"
msgstr ""
"Setelah Alice dan Bob memilih kasus-kasus di mana mereka menggunakan basis "
"pengukuran yang sama, berapa persen bit informasi tersebut yang seharusnya "
"cocok, jika noise dan kesalahan kuantum diabaikan?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume Alice has chosen her measurement bases randomly. Eve also chooses her"
" bases randomly, and she listens in (measures). She sends states on to Bob "
"that are consistent with her measurements. Alice and Bob compare basis "
"choices and keep only the qubits measured/prepared by them in the same "
"bases. Up to some random fluctuation, approximately what percentage of those"
" kept qubit measurements will match, according to Alice and Bob?\n"
msgstr ""
"Asumsikan Alice telah memilih basis pengukurannya secara acak. Eve juga "
"memilih basisnya secara acak, dan dia mendengarkan (mengukur). Eve "
"mengirimkan keadaan ke Bob yang konsisten dengan pengukurannya. Alice dan "
"Bob membandingkan pilihan basis dan hanya menyimpan qubit yang "
"diukur/disiapkan oleh mereka dalam basis yang sama. Dengan mempertimbangkan "
"fluktuasi acak, kira-kira berapa persen pengukuran qubit yang disimpan "
"tersebut yang akan cocok, menurut Alice dan Bob?\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "b. 75%\n"
msgstr "b. 75%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "c. 50%\n"
msgstr "c. 50%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "d. 25%\n"
msgstr "d. 25%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "e. 12.5%\n"
msgstr "e. 12,5%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "f. 0%\n"
msgstr "f. 0%\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Discussion questions {#discussion-questions}"
msgstr "Pertanyaan diskusi {#discussion-questions}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Assume all basis choices are random for all participants, Alice, Bob, and Eve. Assume that after Eve listens in, she sends a state to Bob that is prepared in the same basis in which she measured, and which is consistent with that measurement. Convince your partners that 12.5% of all qubits initialized by Alice will yield measurement mismatches between Alice and Bob, indicating eavesdropping (ignoring quantum errors and noise).\n"
"Hint 1: Since there is no preferred basis, if you consider just one initial choice for Alice, the ratio for that one choice should be the same as the ratio for the sum of all choices.\n"
"Hint 2: It may not be sufficient to count the number of ways something could happen, since some outcomes may occur with different probabilities.\n"
msgstr ""
"1. Asumsikan semua pilihan basis adalah acak untuk semua peserta, Alice, Bob, dan Eve. Asumsikan bahwa setelah Eve mendengarkan, dia mengirimkan keadaan ke Bob yang disiapkan dalam basis yang sama dengan basis pengukurannya, dan yang konsisten dengan pengukuran tersebut. Yakinkan rekan-rekanmu bahwa 12,5% dari semua qubit yang diinisialisasi oleh Alice akan menghasilkan ketidakcocokan pengukuran antara Alice dan Bob, yang mengindikasikan adanya penyadapan (mengabaikan kesalahan dan noise kuantum).\n"
"Petunjuk 1: Karena tidak ada basis yang lebih diutamakan, jika kamu mempertimbangkan hanya satu pilihan awal untuk Alice, rasionya untuk satu pilihan tersebut seharusnya sama dengan rasio untuk jumlah semua pilihan.\n"
"Petunjuk 2: Mungkin tidak cukup hanya menghitung jumlah cara sesuatu bisa terjadi, karena beberapa hasil mungkin terjadi dengan probabilitas yang berbeda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume again that all basis choices are random for all participants, Alice, "
"Bob, and Eve. But now, consider that Eve is free to send along any state she"
" likes after her measurement. She could even try sending states that are "
"inconsistent with her own measurements. Discuss with your partners/neighbors"
" whether you think there is any choice of bases that could reduce the "
"average percentage of qubits that indicate eavesdropping to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Asumsikan lagi bahwa semua pilihan basis adalah acak untuk semua peserta, "
"Alice, Bob, dan Eve. Namun sekarang, pertimbangkan bahwa Eve bebas "
"mengirimkan keadaan apa pun yang dia suka setelah pengukurannya. Eve bahkan "
"bisa mencoba mengirimkan keadaan yang tidak konsisten dengan pengukurannya "
"sendiri. Diskusikan dengan rekan/tetangga kamu apakah menurutmu ada pilihan "
"basis yang bisa mengurangi persentase rata-rata qubit yang mengindikasikan "
"penyadapan kepada Alice dan Bob.\n"
